From 64cbf2c8ac5e799100acbfcf339682e7971f7c2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:51:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] system stack: listen again when Android destroys the TCP
 listener

Android can destroy the listening socket on the TUN address
(SOCK_DESTROY, seen on OxygenOS 16 when the VPN is rebuilt). The accept
loop then returned silently and every new TCP connection was refused
until the stack restarted, while UDP and ICMP kept working. Listen again
on the same address and port instead.
---
